---

# 16. AI Business Assistant

The AI Assistant helps users by:

- Recording sales
- Recording expenses
- Recording payments
- Searching customers
- Searching products
- Explaining reports
- Answering business questions
- Guiding first-time users

The AI should communicate professionally and concisely.

---

# 17. Daily Business Brief

The AI generates a daily summary.

Example:

Today's Sales

Today's Expenses

Outstanding Credit

New Customers

Top Selling Products

Low Activity Alerts

Business Recommendations

Daily Briefs are generated from confirmed business data only.

---

# 18. AI Recommendations

The AI may proactively suggest:

- Follow up overdue customers.
- Frequently purchased products.
- Best-selling products.
- Slow-moving products.
- High-spending customers.
- Unusual expenses.
- Duplicate customer detection.
- Duplicate product detection.

Recommendations are advisory only.

The user decides whether to act.

---

# 19. Business Analytics AI

The AI provides intelligent analysis such as:

Sales Trends

Revenue Growth

Expense Breakdown

Customer Purchase Behaviour

Payment Trends

Monthly Performance

Future modules may include:

Demand Forecasting

Profit Forecasting

Cash Flow Prediction

Customer Churn Prediction

---

# 20. AI Guardrails

The AI must never:

- Invent customers.
- Invent products.
- Invent prices.
- Invent payment amounts.
- Invent balances.
- Modify financial records without confirmation.
- Delete records automatically.
- Override business rules.
- Ignore the Rules Engine.
- Guess missing financial information.

Whenever information is incomplete, the AI asks for clarification.

---

# 21. Security and Privacy

The AI processes only data that the authenticated user is authorised to access.

The AI:

- Respects Row Level Security.
- Never bypasses permissions.
- Never exposes another business's data.
- Never stores confidential information outside approved storage.
- Never trains foundation models using customer business data without explicit consent.

---

# 22. AI Auditability

Every AI-assisted action records:

- User
- Timestamp
- Request
- AI interpretation
- Confidence scores
- User confirmation
- Final action
- Outcome

These records support troubleshooting and compliance.

---

# 23. Error Handling

When confidence is low:

The AI asks for clarification.

When validation fails:

The AI explains the reason and suggests corrective actions.

When an external AI provider is unavailable:

- Notify the user.
- Retry if appropriate.
- Offer manual entry so business operations can continue.

The application should remain usable even if AI services are temporarily unavailable.

---

# 24. Performance Targets

Target response times:

Voice-to-text:

Less than 3 seconds

Intent recognition:

Less than 1 second

AI response:

Less than 5 seconds

Confirmation generation:

Less than 2 seconds

AI processing should never block unrelated application features.

---

# 25. AI Learning Strategy

BizMate AI improves through confirmed user interactions.

The AI may learn:

- Frequently used customer names
- Product aliases
- Preferred transaction wording
- Common business terminology
- User language preferences

The AI must not learn from rejected suggestions or failed validations.

---

